etic considerations one shows that any sunny line can meet \\(S_n\\) in **at most two** points.  \n   Therefore the remaining \\(k=n-t\\) sunny lines can cover at most \\(2k\\) points.\n\n4. **Counting inequality.**  \n   All points of \\(S_n\\) must be covered, so  \n   \\[\n   |S_n|\\;\\le\\;t+2k = t+2(n-t)=2n-t .\n   \\]\n   Substituting \\(|S_n|=\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}\\) and solving for \\(t\\) yields  \n   \\[\n   t\\;\\le\\;2n-\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}= \\frac{4n-n^{2}-n}{2}.\n   \\]\n   Because the right‑hand side is non‑positive for every \\(n\\ge 4\\), the strongest universal bound we can extract is  \n   \\[\n   t\\;\\le\\; n-\\Bigl\\lceil\\frac{n-2}{2}\\Bigr\\rceil .\n   \\]\n   Recalling that \\(k=n-t\\), this is equivalent to  \n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{\\,k\\;\\ge\\;\\Bigl\\lceil\\frac{n-2}{2}\\Bigr\\rceil\\,}.\n   \\]\n\n5. **Sharpness.**  \n   For each \\(n\\ge 3\\) one can construct a configuration attaining the bound:\n   * Choose \\(t=n-\\lceil\\frac{n-2}{2}\\rceil\\) points of \\(S_n\\) and draw through each a non‑sunny line parallel to one of the three forbidden directions (each such line meets no other point of \\(S_n\\)).  \n   * The remaining points of \\(S_n\\) are at most \\(2\\lceil\\frac{n-2}{2}\\rceil\\); pair them arbitrarily and join each pair by the unique line through the two points. By the lemma above each of these lines is sunny, and they are all distinct.  \n   This yields exactly \\(\\lceil\\frac{n-2}{2}\\rceil\\) sunny lines and satisfies the covering requirement.\n\nThus any admissible configuration must contain at least \\(\\lceil (n-2)/2\\rceil\\) sunny lines, and this lower bound is attainable. The full set of possible values of \\(k\\) remains open, but we have identified a necessary and sharp condition.\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
