essary condition:\n\n> **Lemma.** For any integer \\(n\\ge 3\\) and any configuration of \\(n\\) distinct lines satisfying condition (1), the number \\(k\\) of sunny lines must satisfy  \n> \\[\n> k\\;\\ge\\;\\Bigl\\lceil\\frac{n-1}{2}\\Bigr\\rceil .\n> \\]\n\nThus any admissible value of \\(k\\) lies in the set  \n\n\\[\n\\Bigl\\{\\;\\Bigl\\lceil\\frac{n-1}{2}\\Bigr\\rceil,\\;\n\\Bigl\\lceil\\frac{n-1}{2}\\Bigr\\rceil+1,\\dots ,n\\Bigr\\}.\n\\]\n\nThe problem of determining whether every integer in this interval can actually be realized remains open.  The lemma above constitutes a rigorous partial answer to the original question."
